{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>לחמנו</b> — four times in the Masorah: כי לחמנו הם, לחמנו נאכל, זה לחמנו חם, הצטיידנו בנפשנו נביא לחמנו. If in YHWH you do not rebel — לחמנו הם ונאכלם כלחם. But after they transgressed the word of YHWH, ויכום ויכתום, and this is: בנפשנו נביא לחמנו — by the sword of the wilderness. And the journey was exceedingly long for them, for they walked forty years in the wilderness."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The four citations are unaddressed in the source; the first three are identifiable (Numbers 14:9, Deuteronomy 2:28, Joshua 9:12 respectively) but the fourth, הצטיידנו בנפשנו נביא לחמנו, does not correspond to any known biblical verse and may reflect a variant or corrupted citation. The phrase ויכום ויכתום is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'and they struck them and they crushed them.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:09.556836455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}